 three E’s (environment, economy, and equity). The goal of this course is to elicit discussion, stimulate independent thinking, and encourage students to understand and challenge the “conventional wisdom” of transportation planning.", "course_url": "https://ocw.mit.edu/courses/1-252j-urban-transportation-planning-fall-2016/", "image_url": "https://ocw.mit.edu/courses/1-252j-urban-transportation-planning-fall-2016/da01775110f44dcb70ce6a87159c9ef3_1-252F16.jpg", "license_name": "CC BY-NC-SA 4.0", "license_url": "https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc-sa/4.0/", "resources": {"syllabus": true, "calendar": true, "readings": true, "lecture_notes": true, "assignments": true, "projects": false, "exams": false, "videos": false, "instructor_insights": true, "related_resources": false}, "metadata_origin": {"subject_primary": "source", "subject_secondary": "source", "academic_levels": "source", "course_feature_tags": "source"}, "capture_date": "2026-10-03", "last_verified_date": "2026-10-03", "extraction_status": "complete"}, "resources": [{"resource_id": "mitocw-1-252j-fall-2016-course-home", "course_id": "mitocw-1-252j-fall-2016", "resource_type": "course_home", "source_title": "Course Description", "source_url": "https://ocw.mit.edu/courses/1-252j-urban-transportation-planning-fall-2016/", "source_format": "html", "availability": "available", "extraction_policy": "full_text", "extraction_status": "complete", "local_path": "course-description.md", "capture_date": "2026-10-03", "content_sha256": "cad54dc28a2356dbe203c9b3a5bda098dddb794a175449774f022eeb2cfe6896", "error": null}, {"resource_id": "mitocw-1-252j-fall-2016-syllabus", "course_id": "mitocw-1-252j-fall-2016", "resource_type": "syllabus", "source_title": "Syllabus", "source_url": "https://ocw.mit.edu/courses/1-252j-urban-transportation-planning-fall-2016/pages/syllabus/", "source_format": "html", "availability": "available", "extraction_policy": "full_text", "extraction_status": "complete", "local_path": "syllabus.